<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Pathway xmlns="http://pathvisio.org/GPML/2021" title="cadmium transport I" organism="cellular organisms" source="PlantCyc" version="20260303222105">
  <Xref identifier="PWY-6213" dataSource="MetaCyc" />
  <Description>Heavy metal transporters are involved acquisition and compartmentation, metal absorption and detoxication. In food crops and economically important plants the excess accumulation of heavy metals is a severe problem and affects yields. On the other hand plants are used to remove excess metal contamination from soils in a process called bioremediation |CITS: [15013746]|. This pathway describes the transporter involved in the transport of |FRAME: CD+2 Cd&lt;SUP&gt;2+&lt;/SUP&gt;|.</Description>
  <Authors>
    <Author name="PMN" />
    <Author name="zhang" />
    <Author name="O-28" />
    <Author name="pujar" />
  </Authors>
